# builtin-is-contractive: returns true for a plain Int value.
--- uses: ["core"]
# The contractiveness check falls to the default arm (Case 2): any value that is
# neither TypeNode.RecursiveRef nor TypeNode.Union/Intersect is treated as guarding.
# This represents the leaf case — primitive TypeNode constructors (Int, Float, Bool,
# String, etc.) are all guarding, so any path through them to a RecursiveRef is safe.
[result: [builtin-is-contractive 42]]
=== out
Dict({"result": Int(1)})
